@ 9:8  cur|ve: basis
  9:5-9:10 "curve"
  | **flowchart.curve**
  |
  | How flowchart edges are drawn between their route points (D733).
  |
  | Defaults to `rounded`: right angles whose corners are small arcs.
  | Precedence: a per-edge curve (`curve:` on an edge, `linkStyle …
  | interpolate`), then this key when set, then the top-level `curve`
  | when set, then `rounded`. A swimlane diagram reads `swimlane.curve`
  | first. The top-level `curve` and every `<type>.curve` take these names.
  |
  | Type: `"basis" | "bumpX" | "bumpY" | "cardinal" | "catmullRom" | "linear" | "monotoneX" | "monotoneY" | "natural" | "step" | "stepAfter" | "stepBefore" | "rounded"`
  |
  | Status: honoured (since 13.0.0). The default changes from `basis` to `rounded`, the look of v12's default ELK layout: stepped routes whose corners are arcs of radius 5 (less on a short leg). Set `basis` to keep S-curves. `linear` draws straight segments; `step`, `stepBefore` and `stepAfter` draw stepped routes with right-angle corners (the step in the middle, near the start and near the end of the leg); `rounded` draws straight segments with rounded corners; every other value draws S-curves (the layout engine routes edges, not a d3 curve factory). A name outside this list is drawn with the default, `rounded`, and warns `CURVE_UNKNOWN` once per render (D602, D681); v12 drew it as `basis`. The default lives in code, not in the schema (D733), so the resolved config shows no `flowchart.curve` unless it is set, and the top-level `curve` applies where it is not.
@ 10:13  htmlLabe|ls: true
  10:5-10:15 "htmlLabels"
  | **flowchart.htmlLabels**
  |
  | **DEPRECATED: Use global `htmlLabels` instead.**
  |
  | Flag for setting whether or not a html tag should be used for rendering labels on nodes and edges.
  | This property is deprecated.
  | Please use the global `htmlLabels` configuration instead.
  |
  | Type: `boolean | null` · Default: `null`
  |
  | Status: removed (since 13.0.0). Core draws labels as SVG text only (D5). Replacement: the HTML labels plugin, which reads the key as `html.labels` (D694, D696).
